From: Kinolune contributors
Subject: [PATCH] meson: build utils-mac.c for CoreAudio without cocoa

ao_coreaudio_utils.c and ao_coreaudio_properties.c call cfstr_from_cstr()
and cfstr_get_cstr() from osdep/utils-mac.c, but that file is only built
with the cocoa feature. Our macOS libmpv is built with auto_features
disabled and no cocoa, so the two symbols stayed undefined, were linked as
dynamic_lookup and resolved to NULL: listing audio devices (the
audio-device-list property media_kit observes) crashed the app with
SIGSEGV at address 0. utils-mac.c needs only CoreFoundation. Not sent
upstream yet.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -880,6 +880,12 @@
 if features['audiounit'] or features['coreaudio'] or features['avfoundation']
     sources += files('audio/out/ao_coreaudio_chmap.c',
                      'audio/out/ao_coreaudio_utils.c')
+    # cfstr_from_cstr/cfstr_get_cstr live in osdep/utils-mac.c, which is only
+    # built with cocoa. Without cocoa the CoreAudio outputs linked them as
+    # unresolved dynamic_lookup symbols and crashed on a NULL call.
+    if not features['cocoa']
+        sources += files('osdep/utils-mac.c')
+    endif
 endif
 
 if features['avfoundation']
